Maintainer: G-Helper contributors <ghelper@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/bberka/g-helper
Depends: libc6, libgcc-s1, libstdc++6, zlib1g, libfontconfig1, libx11-6, libice6, libsm6
Recommends: pkexec | policykit-1, xdg-utils, power-profiles-daemon
Description: Control tool for ASUS laptops (performance modes, fans, GPU mode, battery limit, lighting)
 Cross-platform fork of G-Helper: performance modes, fan curves, power limits,
 GPU mode, battery charge limit, keyboard lighting and ASUS peripherals through
 the asus-wmi kernel driver. Self-contained: ships its own .NET runtime.
 .
 Installs udev rules and a polkit action; members of the "ghelper" group (and
 the user logged in at the seat) can access the hardware without root.
 Needs ICU (libicuNN) for localisation; without it start with
 DOTNET_SYSTEM_GLOBALIZATION_INVARIANT=1.
